# Runtime dependency FLOORS. Not what production installs — see below.
#
# requirements.txt is compiled from this file by pip-compile and pins every
# resolved version, transitive ones included, together with its artifact hashes
# (audit KRY-007). Install that, never this:
#
#     pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt
#
# Regenerate after editing this file — under Python 3.12, the version CI checks
# freshness with, since markers can resolve differently on another interpreter:
#
#     pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# The .in -> .txt pair is pip-compile's own convention, and it is chosen for
# Dependabot: it recognises the pair and regenerates the hashed file in the same
# PR. The previous requirements.txt (floors) -> requirements.lock pair was not
# recognised, so every Dependabot pip PR bumped a floor, left the lock behind,
# failed the freshness check, and could not land without manual work — which is
# how the security gate came to stay red on main (audit 2026-10-12 K-11).
